        "text": "All the requested Python files have been created successfully in the current working directory. Here are the files and their purposes:\n\n1. **[SAME-SCENARIO] synthesize_text.py** - Synthesizes plain text to an audio byte stream using Microsoft Azure Cognitive Services.\n2. **[SAME-SCENARIO] synthesize_ssml.py** - Synthesizes SSML with voice and prosody controls using Microsoft Azure Cognitive Services.\n3. **[SAME-SCENARIO] select_voice.py** - Lists or selects a voice for a target locale using Microsoft Azure Cognitive Services.\n4. **[SAME-SCENARIO] save_audio.py** - Writes synthesized speech audio to a local file using Microsoft Azure Cognitive Services.\n5. **[HELPER] speech_client.py** - Provides local configuration and client helper utilities for Text-to-Speech using Microsoft Azure Cognitive Services.\n6. **[HELPER] speech_models.py** - Defines local request, response, and normalization helpers for Text-to-Speech using Microsoft Azure Cognitive Services.\n7. **[LATER-STEP] script_translate.py** - Placeholder for translating narration scripts before synthesis.\n8. **[LATER-STEP] script_safety.py** - Placeholder for checking narration scripts for unsafe content.\n9. **[LATER-STEP] script_embedding.py** - Placeholder for embedding narration scripts for voice-asset search.\n10. **[LATER-STEP] tts_qa_transcript.py** - Placeholder for transcribing synthesized QA samples to verify spoken output.\n\nEach scored implementation file uses Microsoft Azure Cognitive Services as the concrete external provider and makes it identifiable in the code. The local helper files provide configuration loading, payload normalization, or response parsing utilities when useful.",
